1. JavaScript Object

A JavaScript Object is a collection of related data and functionality stored as key-value pairs. The data is represented by properties and the actions are represented by methods.

JavaScript Object related data और functionality का collection होता है, जिसमें data को key-value pairs के रूप में store किया जाता है। Object के data को properties और उसके actions को methods कहा जाता है।

Example
const student = {
    name: "Adyut",
    age: 21,
    course: "BCA"
};

name   → property/key
Adyut   → value
age    → property/key
21     → value
course → property/key
BCA    → value

2. why use Object -> 
Objects are used to group related information and functions together in a single structure.
Objects का उपयोग related information और functions को एक ही structure में रखने के लिए किया जाता है।

Example

Student information:

const student = {
    name: "Adyut",
    rollNo: 101,
    course: "BCA",
    marks: 85
};

//one student related all info store single object structure

3. Object Properties -> An object property is a named value stored inside an object.
Object Property object के अंदर store की गई named value होती है।

Example
const student = {
    name: "Adyut",
    age: 21,
    course: "BCA"
};

Property Access

The two main ways to access an object's property in programming (like in JavaScript) are Dot notation and Bracket notation.

1. Dot Notation -> You use a dot (.) followed by the property name. It is the most common, clean, and readable way to access properties.

Syntax
object.property
const user = { name: "Alice", age: 25 };
// Accessing property
console.log(user.name); // Output: Alice

2. Bracket Notation -> You use square brackets ([]) and pass the property name as a string. This method is more powerful and flexible.

Syntax
object["property"]

const user = { 
  name: "Alice", 
  "home address": "123 Street" // Key with a space
};

// Accessing property with a space
console.log(user["home address"]); // Output: 123 Street

// Accessing property using a variable
const key = "name";
console.log(user[key]); // Output: Alice


4. Object Methods ->An object method is a function stored as a property of an object.
Object Method वह function है जो object की property के रूप में stored होता है।

Example
const student = {
    name: "Adyut",
    show: function() {
        console.log("Student Name:", this.name);
    }
};

student.show();

5. this Object -> The this keyword refers to the object that is currently calling the method.
this keyword उस object को refer करता है जो वर्तमान में method को call कर रहा है।

Example
const student = {
    name: "Adyut",
    showName: function() {
        console.log(this.name);
    }
};
student.showName();

Easy Concept
student.showName()
       ↓
     this
       ↓
    student
       ↓
 this.name
       ↓
