Step 6 – Object Protection

JavaScript में object को unwanted changes से protect करने के लिए तीन important methods हैं:

Object.preventExtensions()
Object.seal()
Object.freeze()
27. Object.preventExtensions()
English Definition

Object.preventExtensions() prevents new properties from being added to an object.

Hindi Definition

Object.preventExtensions() object में नई properties add होने से रोकता है, लेकिन existing properties को generally modify या delete किया जा सकता है।

Example
const student = {
    name: "Adyut"
};

Object.preventExtensions(student);

student.age = 21;

student.name = "Rahul";

console.log(student);

Conceptually:

age → Add नहीं होगी
name → Change हो सकती है
28. Object.seal()
English Definition

Object.seal() prevents adding or deleting properties, but existing property values can generally still be changed if they are writable.

Hindi Definition

Object.seal() नई properties add करने और existing properties delete करने से रोकता है, लेकिन writable existing properties की values बदली जा सकती हैं।

Example
const student = {
    name: "Adyut",
    age: 21
};

Object.seal(student);

student.name = "Rahul";

delete student.age;

student.course = "BCA";

console.log(student);

Result:

name change → Allowed
delete       → Not allowed
new property → Not allowed
29. Object.freeze()
English Definition

Object.freeze() prevents adding, deleting, or changing properties of an object.

Hindi Definition

Object.freeze() object में properties को add, delete या modify करने से रोकता है।

Example
const student = {
    name: "Adyut",
    age: 21
};

Object.freeze(student);

student.name = "Rahul";

student.age = 25;

student.course = "BCA";

delete student.age;

console.log(student);

Object की original properties change नहीं होंगी।

30. Protection Difference
| Method                | Add | Delete | Change |
| --------------------- | --: | -----: | -----: |
| Normal Object         |   ✅ |      ✅ |      ✅ |
| `preventExtensions()` |   ❌ |      ✅ |      ✅ |
| `seal()`              |   ❌ |      ❌ |      ✅ |
| `freeze()`            |   ❌ |      ❌ |      ❌ |


Step 7 – Prototypes
31. JavaScript Prototype
English Definition

A prototype is an object from which another object can inherit properties and methods.

Hindi Definition

Prototype एक ऐसा object है जिससे दूसरा object properties और methods को inherit कर सकता है।

Important Concept

JavaScript objects have a prototype chain through which inherited properties and methods can be accessed.

Example
const person = {

    greet: function() {
        console.log("Hello");
    }

};

const student = Object.create(person);

student.name = "Adyut";

student.greet();

Output:

Hello

student के अंदर directly greet() नहीं है, लेकिन वह अपने prototype person से इसे access करता है।

32. Prototype Chain
student
   ↓
student's prototype
   ↓
person
   ↓
Object.prototype
   ↓
null
Hindi

जब JavaScript को कोई property या method object में directly नहीं मिलती, तो वह prototype chain में ऊपर search कर सकती है।

33. Constructor और Prototype
function Student(name) {

    this.name = name;

}

Student.prototype.show = function() {

    console.log("Name:", this.name);

};

const student1 = new Student("Adyut");

student1.show();

Output:

Name: Adyut
Explanation

English: show() is stored on the constructor's prototype and can be accessed by objects created using new Student().

Hindi: show() constructor के prototype पर रखा गया है और new Student() से बनाए गए objects इसे access कर सकते हैं।

